  "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows: \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+0x-4\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+36 \\\\  & x-6\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-4} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-36x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,36x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{36x-216}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,212\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
